/arc-plc/new-york/dutchess-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record for Dutchess County runs from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 10 grids August to September came in under 90% of normal in 38 of 75 years, more than any other pair. In 2025 that pair came in at 68% of normal, and January to February was at 58%. So far in 2026, May to June stands at 61% and June to July at 119% on the middle of the grids. Grid 26025 had its driest year in 1964 at 63% of normal.</p>"}
